From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:56:11 -0500
Subject: fix: raise a Space's floating name after the layout, not in it

Removing a closed row synthesizes a mouse move inside the window's layout
(TabCollectionAnimatingLayoutManager::RemoveNonAnimatingPendingDeleteViews). A
chip that took its first hover there floated its name with ReorderChildView on
the sidebar, whose layout was walking those children: CHECK(!iterating_), in
every build. It takes a pointer on a chip that has not been told so, and a name
not yet the last child. AddressSanitizer's run of 0.4.0 beta 11 hit it once in
CommandBarActionsTest.EveryRowRuns.

The name is raised a turn later, and only when it is not last already.

Why: a hover must not stop the browser (BACKLOG S-440, sidebar Y14).

Removable when: the floating name no longer needs to be last among the
sidebar's children.
---
 .../frame/vertical_tab_strip_region_view.cc   | 18 +++++-
 .../frame/vertical_tab_strip_region_view.h    |  2 +
 .../test/stedding/space_switch_browsertest.cc | 61 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 79 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/vertical_tab_strip_region_view.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/vertical_tab_strip_region_view.cc
index 929e1783f407a..a574d859a54d1 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/vertical_tab_strip_region_view.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/vertical_tab_strip_region_view.cc
@@ -4195,8 +4195,22 @@ void VerticalTabStripRegionView::OnSpaceChipHovered(
   const int y = chip_in_view.y() - height - 4;
   space_hover_pill_->SetBoundsRect(gfx::Rect(x, y, width, height));
   space_hover_pill_->SetVisible(true);
-  // Above the chips in paint order.
-  ReorderChildView(space_hover_pill_, children().size() - 1);
+  // Above the chips in paint order. A turn later: the hover can come in this
+  // view's own layout, from the move Chromium synthesizes when a closed row
+  // goes, and children cannot be reordered while they are walked (BACKLOG
+  // S-440).
+  if (children().back().get() != space_hover_pill_.get()) {
+    base::SingleThreadTaskRunner::GetCurrentDefault()->PostTask(
+        FROM_HERE,
+        base::BindOnce(&VerticalTabStripRegionView::RaiseSpaceHoverPill,
+                       weak_factory_.GetWeakPtr()));
+  }
+}
+
+void VerticalTabStripRegionView::RaiseSpaceHoverPill() {
+  if (space_hover_pill_) {
+    ReorderChildView(space_hover_pill_, children().size() - 1);
+  }
 }
 
